    "text": "Let the (soluble) group G = AB with finite torsion-free rank r0 (G) be the\nproduct of two subgroups A and B. Is the equation r0 (G) = r0 (A)+r0 (B)−r0 (A∩B)\nvalid in this case? It is known that the inequality ⩽ always holds.     B. Amberg",
